1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:02,931
This AI model can't write a single sentence.

2
00:00:02,971 --> 00:00:06,021
And that's exactly why you need it.

3
00:00:06,125 --> 00:00:09,560
Most of what your AI does all day is tiny decisions.

4
00:00:09,663 --> 00:00:11,925
Yes or no. Warm or cold.

5
00:00:12,029 --> 00:00:14,329
And you're paying Opus prices for them.

6
00:00:14,433 --> 00:00:17,040
It's called Jev, from TypeSafe AI.

7
00:00:17,144 --> 00:00:19,752
About 4 cents per million input tokens.

8
00:00:19,856 --> 00:00:21,079
Output is free.

9
00:00:21,452 --> 00:00:23,021
Four ways to use it.

10
00:00:23,298 --> 00:00:24,470
One. Route first.

11
00:00:24,510 --> 00:00:28,489
Jev Router picks the model and the reasoning effort for every request.

12
00:00:28,529 --> 00:00:30,983
And it's live on OpenRouter.

13
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,348
Two. Triage.

14
00:00:32,452 --> 00:00:34,329
Send it a hundred lead emails.

15
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:37,598
It tags each one warm, cold or not a lead.

16
00:00:37,702 --> 00:00:39,579
Claude only writes the warm replies.

17
00:00:39,952 --> 00:00:41,329
Three. Score.

18
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:42,540
Give it a rubric.

19
00:00:42,644 --> 00:00:46,271
It scores every ticket and tells you how confident it is.

20
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:48,204
Four. Guardrails.

21
00:00:48,308 --> 00:00:51,069
One true or false check before anything ships.

22
00:00:51,404 --> 00:00:54,185
Claude does the thinking. Jev makes the calls.

23
00:00:54,288 --> 00:00:57,608
It's early access, so test it on your own workflow first.

24
00:00:57,712 --> 00:00:59,262
Links are in the pinned comment.
